Description:

The dlist parser now rejects file literals unless the caller has explicitly
allowed them, which only the replication protocol does.  Previously a dlist
parsed from stored metadata -- an annotation, for instance -- could hold a
file literal, and parsing it wrote a file to disk containing the bytes that
followed the literal.  Parsing an annotation no longer creates files.

Tracked as GitHub security advisory GHSA-v644-h89x-hwgx.


